title Kubernetes cluster
direction down

Users [icon: users]
Cloud load balancer [icon: load-balancer]

Cluster [icon: kubernetes, color: blue] {
  Control plane [icon: k8s-control-plane, color: gray] {
    API server [icon: k8s-api-server]
    Scheduler [icon: cog]
    Controller manager [icon: settings]
    etcd [icon: k8s-etcd, shape: cylinder]
  }
  Ingress namespace [icon: k8s-namespace] {
    Ingress controller [icon: k8s-ingress, description: NGINX]
  }
  App namespace [icon: k8s-namespace, color: green] {
    Web deployment [icon: k8s-deployment] {
      Web pod 1 [icon: k8s-pod]
      Web pod 2 [icon: k8s-pod]
      Web pod 3 [icon: k8s-pod]
    }
    Web service [icon: k8s-service]
    API deployment [icon: k8s-deployment] {
      API pod 1 [icon: k8s-pod]
      API pod 2 [icon: k8s-pod]
    }
    API service [icon: k8s-service]
    Config [icon: k8s-configmap]
    Secrets [icon: k8s-secret]
    Autoscaler [icon: k8s-hpa]
  }
  Data namespace [icon: k8s-namespace, color: purple] {
    Postgres [icon: k8s-statefulset, description: StatefulSet]
    Volume [icon: k8s-pvc]
  }
}

Users > Cloud load balancer > Ingress controller
Ingress controller > Web service
Web service > Web pod 1, Web pod 2, Web pod 3
Web pod 1, Web pod 2, Web pod 3 > API service
API service > API pod 1, API pod 2
API pod 1, API pod 2 > Postgres
Postgres - Volume
API deployment -- Config, Secrets
Autoscaler --> API deployment: scales
API server <> etcd
Scheduler, Controller manager > API server
